.TH ESC4HTML 1 "2026-09-04" "esc4html" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esc4html \- escape text for inclusion in HTML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esc4html
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esc4html
reads text from standard input, escapes HTML special characters, and writes the
result to standard output.
It replaces
.BR & ,
.BR < ,
.BR > ,
.BR \(dq ,
and
.B \(aq
with their corresponding character references.
.PP
Existing character references are escaped again.
For example,
.B &amp;
becomes
.BR &amp;amp; .
.PP
The command accepts no options or file operands.
Use input redirection to read from a file.
.PP
.B esc4html
does not parse or sanitize HTML.
It can escape text for inclusion in HTML text nodes and ordinary quoted HTML
attribute values.
It does not validate attribute values that have their own syntax, such as URLs,
CSS, or JavaScript.
.SH EXAMPLES
Use the command in a pipeline:
.PP
.nf
.RS
somecmd | esc4html | somecmd
.RE
.fi
.PP
Escape a file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
esc4html < in.txt > out.txt
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The input was processed successfully.
.TP
.B 2
One or more command-line arguments were supplied.
.PP
Any other value indicates an error reported by
.BR sed (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sed (1),
.BR sh (1)
